  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1480714378408-67cf0d13bc1b?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Money functions as experience in Yakuza 0—every yen earned goes toward style upgrades. Prioritise Thug Style (Kiryu) for the Rush Combo extension and Beast Style launch attack, which together cover most combat scenarios.",
      "The Real Estate (Kiryu) and Cabaret Club (Majima) sub-games are the primary end-game money generation systems—invest in real estate properties to generate passive income, then use that income to fund premium hostess upgrades.",
      "CP (Completion Points) are earned from substories and minigames—spend CP exclusively on Ability upgrades (dragon abilities tree) rather than style skill unlocks, which are cheaper via money grinding.",
      "The coliseum (Martial Arts Tournaments) unlocks premium materials not available elsewhere—compete after reaching Chapter 9 when your combat kit is fully developed to clear S-class tournaments.",
      "Substories (side quests) disappear permanently after certain story chapters—complete all Kamurocho substories before Chapter 10 and all Sotenbori substories before Chapter 13 to avoid permanent misses."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "お金は龍が如く0でスタイルアップグレードに使用される経験値として機能する。サブコンテンツと戦闘コンボ拡張のために喧嘩スタイル（桐生）のラッシュコンボ拡張と野獣スタイルの打ち上げ攻撃を優先する。",
      "不動産（桐生）とキャバレークラブ（真島）のサブゲームは主要な終盤の資金生成システム。不動産物件に投資して受動的な収入を生み出し、その収入を使って高品質のホステスのアップグレードに資金を提供する。",
      "CP（クリア実績ポイント）はサブストーリーとミニゲームから獲得する。お金のグラインドで安く解放できるスタイルのスキルアンロックではなく、アビリティアップグレード（ドラゴンの能力ツリー）専用にCPを使用する。",
      "コロシアム（武術大会）は他では入手できないプレミアム素材をロック解除する。戦闘キットが完全に開発された第9章後に競技し、Sクラストーナメントをクリアする。",
      "サブストーリー（サイドクエスト）は特定のストーリー章後に永久に消える。永久的な見逃しを避けるため、第10章前に神室町のサブストーリーを全て完了し、第13章前に蒼天堀のサブストーリーを完了する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Chapter 1–3 Combat Style Priorities",
        "body": "Kiryu starts with Brawler Style unlocked. Invest first in Brawler's Heat Action tree for the heat-activated grab-stomp (most efficient crowd control early game). Majima starts with Breaker Style—invest in Breaker's combo extensions first as they chain into faster Slugger Style transitions. Do not invest in the Dragon of Dojima or Mad Dog of Shimano Styles until Chapter 8 when they become available; spending money on inaccessible style trees is a common early mistake."
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Money Farming Loop",
        "body": "The fastest early money loop (Chapters 3–6): complete telephone club mini-game in Kamurocho to unlock premium clients → collect phone call mini-game rewards (each completed call chain earns 1–5 million yen) → invest in the lowest-priced real estate property available → return income toward the next property. The telephone club is available from Chapter 3 and has zero combat requirement, making it the most accessible passive income trigger before the real estate system opens fully."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Real Estate and Cabaret Club Management",
        "body": "Real estate generates income every 5 in-game minutes regardless of player activity—purchase all 9 properties in each Kamurocho district before expanding to other areas to stack income from a single district. The Cabaret Club requires active minigame management: assign hostesses based on client type (aggressive clients need Bold hostesses; shy clients need Demure hostesses). Maxed Platinum-class hostess earns 10× more per session than standard hostesses."
      },
      {
        "title": "Combat Style Switching in Boss Fights",
        "body": "Style switching mid-combo (hold bumper to switch) is the primary skill gap in Yakuza 0 combat. Most boss encounters cycle between vulnerable states: when knocked back (Beast Style window), when standing still (Thug Rush window), when blocking (Brawler Grab window). The optimal switching pattern: Thug Rush to stagger → Beast Style one heavy hit → Thug Rush continuation before guard recovery. This loop deals 40% more damage per time unit than any single-style approach."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dragon of Dojima and Mad Dog Mastery",
        "body": "Dragon of Dojima Style (Kiryu, Chapter 8+) and Mad Dog of Shimano Style (Majima, Chapter 8+) are the final, strongest styles. Both require significant investment to unlock their most useful moves. Dragon of Dojima's Tiger Drop counter (parry move) is the highest-damage single combo starter in the game—the counter activates on any non-grab attack with a 3-frame window. Mad Dog's Dance of the Mad Dog combo extension provides invincibility frames during the early hits, functioning as an offensive dodge."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Spending all money on style upgrades before unlocking real estate—real estate provides returns that exceed combat upgrade value within 30 minutes; unlock real estate first before investing in expensive style capstones.",
      "Ignoring the completion list—the completion list tracks every side activity and provides CP that funds the most powerful ability upgrades; checking it at the start of each chapter ensures no time-sensitive activities are missed.",
      "Fighting inside interiors without switching to Thug Style—Beast Style ragdolls enemies into furniture, causing environmental damage but also removing them from your combo range; use Thug or Brawler in tight indoor environments.",
      "Skipping the Karaoke and telephone club substories—these substories provide unique Heat Actions not available from style trees and are permanently missable after Chapters 10 and 12 respectively.",
      "Not using Heat Actions against bosses—Heat Actions are the highest single-burst damage options in any encounter; triggering them during boss vulnerability windows deals 3–5× normal attack damage and often causes instant knockdowns."
    ],
